From c912805f76f018c93416164c52753e5a98ba7d25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Schmitz <jan.schmitz@whu.edu>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 15:17:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] harden XSS script-block, promote tag normalization, fix
 SSRF/file-size/auth-timing

Follow-ups from the composer/media-library XSS fix plus broader audit findings:

* compose.html script block: replace four |safe JSON interpolations with
  Django's |json_script + JSON.parse, closing the </script>-breakout vector
  inside Alpine's composerApp.
* Promote _normalize_tags + constants to apps/common/validators.py. Add
  parse_and_truncate_tag_string and parse_and_truncate_youtube_tag_string
  helpers for lenient (form POST) paths. Apply across composer save_post,
  autosave, idea_create, idea_update, and YouTube yt_tags.
* Add HTTP-level integration tests for media-library tag endpoints and
  composer save_post (including XSS round-trip + json_script container
  assertions).
* SSRF: validate RSS feed URLs and notification webhook URLs against
  private/loopback/link-local IPs via is_safe_url; manual redirect handling
  with per-hop re-validation on the RSS path.
* CSV upload: cap at 5 MB before reading into memory.
* Calendar slot delete/update: scope the get_object_or_404 query to the
  workspace so cross-workspace slot IDs return 404 from the DB lookup,
  not from a post-lookup ownership check.
* Inline comment on apps/onboarding/checklist.py:icon_svg noting that the
  field must remain a server-side constant (rendered with |safe).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
